DOQS — Licence overview

This repository is the Documentation System: validators, schemas, templates,
and the canonical architecture specification. It is not a hardware machine
repo.

Each kind of content is licensed separately. Full legal texts are in
[`LICENSES/`](LICENSES/); this file explains which licence applies where.

Machine repositories that include this repo as a `doqs/` submodule use a
different, three-way split (CERN-OHL-S hardware, GPL-3.0 firmware/software,
CC BY-SA docs). That layout is documented in
[`docs/architecture.md`](docs/architecture.md#licensing) and written by
`scripts/apply_licenses.py`. Templates for those files live in
[`templates/licensing/`](templates/licensing/).

## Software — GPL-3.0

Applies to: [`scripts/`](scripts/), [`schemas/`](schemas/), [`tests/`](tests/)
(except the machine-repo fixture, see below), and other original source code
in this repository.

Full text: [`LICENSES/GPL-3.0.txt`](LICENSES/GPL-3.0.txt)

## Documentation — CC BY-SA 4.0

Applies to: [`docs/`](docs/), [`templates/`](templates/), [`data/`](data/),
this file, README, CONTRIBUTING, and other project-authored documentation.

Excluded: third-party material that is not authored by this project remains
under its original copyright. In particular:

- [`spec/otrl.ttl`](spec/otrl.ttl) is copied from
  [iop-alliance/OpenKnowHow](https://github.com/iop-alliance/OpenKnowHow)
  and is GPL-3.0-or-later (see the file header).
- Legal texts under [`templates/licensing/LICENSES/`](templates/licensing/LICENSES/)
  are the CERN-OHL-S v2.0, GPL-3.0, and CC BY-SA 4.0 documents themselves.

Full text: [`LICENSES/CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt`](LICENSES/CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt)

## Test fixture

[`tests/fixtures/minimal-machine/`](tests/fixtures/minimal-machine/) is a
miniature **machine** repository used by the validators. It uses the machine
content-type split (CERN-OHL-S / GPL-3.0 / CC BY-SA), not the tools-repo
mapping above.

## Directory-level pointers

Each top-level content directory also contains a short `LICENSE` file
restating which of the above applies to that directory.

## Trademarks

The REFAQT name and logo, and the DOQS name and logo, are trademarks and are
not covered by any of the licences above. See
[`TRADEMARKS.md`](TRADEMARKS.md).
